267
00:10:58,060 --> 00:10:59,200
Hold on. This...

268
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,460
It's too small for my head.

269
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:04,770
(Pressing down)

270
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,270
If so, do you want to switch? This is a smaller size.

271
00:11:07,270 --> 00:11:09,310
My head... One moment. I'll try this one on.

272
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:12,780
- Is it okay?
- This one fits me.

273
00:11:12,780 --> 00:11:13,810
- That's good.
- It suits me, right?

274
00:11:13,810 --> 00:11:14,980
It suits you well.

275
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:17,620
You both look good, but I'm too...

276
00:11:17,650 --> 00:11:19,120
It suits you the best.

277
00:11:19,520 --> 00:11:21,550
- Hyun Moo. It's okay.
- Is it okay?

278
00:11:21,750 --> 00:11:24,020
I feel like you'd be on the Pringles container.

279
00:11:24,690 --> 00:11:26,460
- Kind of that vibe.
- Pringles...

280
00:11:27,060 --> 00:11:28,260
Thank you for the gift.

281
00:11:28,260 --> 00:11:29,360
- Thank you.
- Yes.

282
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:30,690
- Shall we walk a bit?
- Yes.

283
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:32,660
This is Stephen Avenue.

284
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:35,500
- Doesn't it look like Myeongdong?
- Oh, my.

285
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:36,670
The busiest place.

286
00:11:41,110 --> 00:11:44,110
(A full view of Calgary Tower, the symbol of Calgary)

287
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:49,310
(A 19th century stone buildings that give off an old-world charm)

288
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:55,490
(A pedestrian area that attracts locals and tourists alike)

289
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:58,660
(Modern energy flows against the old-world background...)

290
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:00,890
(in Stephen Avenue, Calgary's hottest area)

291
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:04,500
When did you last eat?

292
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:07,000
- We haven't eaten since the flight.
- The in-flight meal.

293
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,970
I ate two in-flight meals, and I'm still hungry.

294
00:12:08,970 --> 00:12:10,030
Totally.

295
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:15,140
(Thanks to the cowboy hats,)

296
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:16,410
(the three travel buddies get a warm welcome from locals.)

297
00:12:16,410 --> 00:12:18,110
Cowboy from Korea.

298
00:12:18,110 --> 00:12:20,980
You're such an extrovert, Hyun Moo.

299
00:12:22,650 --> 00:12:24,980
It must be like when foreigners walk around in hanbok.

300
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:26,620
- Right.
- With the tag still on.

301
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:31,890
Since the weather here is nice,

302
00:12:31,890 --> 00:12:33,790
everyone is eating outside. We should too.

303
00:12:33,790 --> 00:12:35,230
This place has the most people.

304
00:12:35,230 --> 00:12:36,960
This place is nice.

305
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:40,260
Shall we try it out?

306
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:41,330
Is there something you want to eat?

307
00:12:41,330 --> 00:12:43,330
Yes, I'm going to try everything.

308
00:12:43,970 --> 00:12:45,040
I'm so hungry.

309
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:49,240
They're all so fascinated by us.

310
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:51,140
- I feel a bit shy.
- Since we're all wearing hats.

311
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:52,580
(They sudden feel shy about everyone looking at them.)

312
00:12:52,580 --> 00:12:53,710
- I feel shy.
- I feel shy.

313
00:12:53,710 --> 00:12:54,980
- All of a sudden.
- Oh, gosh.

314
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:56,110
I feel shy.

315
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,120
Hello.

316
00:12:58,120 --> 00:12:59,380
How are you guys?

317
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:00,890
Good. We have three people.

318
00:13:00,890 --> 00:13:02,420
So, can we eat outside?

319
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:04,020
Yes, we'll get a table for you.

320
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:05,120
- Yes.
- Okay.

321
00:13:07,460 --> 00:13:09,560
(Calgary doesn't sleep.)

322
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:14,670
(This popular Stephen Avenue restaurant...)

323
00:13:14,670 --> 00:13:17,770
(is full of customers enjoying the night.)

324
00:13:19,370 --> 00:13:21,040
- Let's see.
- Yes.

325
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:22,940
- Campanelle?
- Campanelle.

326
00:13:23,340 --> 00:13:24,880
Campanelle is good.

327
00:13:25,110 --> 00:13:28,180
- And the salami pizza is good.
- Okay.

328
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:31,950
And the platter.

329
00:13:32,980 --> 00:13:34,750
- Let's order these first.
- Okay.

330
00:13:35,390 --> 00:13:36,850
Then we can order more if there's something else we want.

331
00:13:36,950 --> 00:13:39,060
- I can eat anything right now.
- Really?

332
00:13:39,060 --> 00:13:40,760
- I'm so hungry right now.
- You're not picky.

333
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:42,330
- You're totally open.
- Yes.

334
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:44,030
You're super open.

335
00:13:44,030 --> 00:13:46,530
Even if they bring me the wrong thing, I eat it.

336
00:13:46,530 --> 00:13:47,530
- Same.
- Really?

337
00:13:47,530 --> 00:13:48,830
- Without complaint.
- Same.

338
00:13:48,830 --> 00:13:50,530
If I order pasta, and they bring me pizza, I eat it.

339
00:13:50,530 --> 00:13:52,270
- Same.
- I get that.

340
00:13:52,270 --> 00:13:54,100
Since you don't want to wait.

341
00:13:54,310 --> 00:13:55,940
- We're going to get along.
- It just has to taste good.

342
00:13:55,940 --> 00:13:57,270
- Exactly.
- Excuse me.

343
00:13:57,270 --> 00:13:58,380
- Campanelle?
- That one's really good.

344
00:13:58,380 --> 00:13:59,510
- That's one of my favourites.
- Okay.

345
00:13:59,510 --> 00:14:00,780
We'll do one of those?

346
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:02,280
Is this to share or individual?

347
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:03,650
- Share.
- Sharing. Okay.

348
00:14:03,650 --> 00:14:05,880
- And the salami pizza.
- Yes.

349
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:07,080
- Is it good?
- Yes, sure.

350
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:08,620
And the...

351
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:10,350
Anything else you recommend?

352
00:14:10,350 --> 00:14:13,190
The calamari is really good. That one is really nice.

353
00:14:13,190 --> 00:14:14,860
- This one too.
- Yes, sure. Sounds good.

354
00:14:14,860 --> 00:14:15,860
- Thank you.
- Anything else...

355
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:16,890
for you guys right now?

356
00:14:16,890 --> 00:14:18,160
I'll have this one.

357
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:19,630
- The Stella? Yes, sure.
- Yes.

358
00:14:19,630 --> 00:14:20,800
The third one.

359
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:22,400
(Joon and Ju Bin also order some beers.)

360
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:23,570
The lager?

361
00:14:23,570 --> 00:14:24,640
- The lager?
- One of those?

362
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:25,640
- Thank you.
- Yes, sure.

363
00:14:26,700 --> 00:14:28,040
I'm so excited.

364
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:29,540
- I'm so hungry.
- I'm hungry.

365
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:30,910
- Oh, I'm so hungry.
- Thank you very much.

366
00:14:30,910 --> 00:14:34,450
It does feel so strange for the three of us,

367
00:14:34,450 --> 00:14:36,380
who have no common ground, to meet in Canada like this.

368
00:14:36,380 --> 00:14:38,020
It's our first time meeting, and it's in Canada.

369
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:39,150
You look like a local right now.

370
00:14:39,150 --> 00:14:40,580
- Really? I...
- This really suits you.

371
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:41,750
I really like it.

372
00:14:42,390 --> 00:14:44,120
- It suits you.
- I really like it.

373
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:45,860
You remind me of "The Good, The Bad, The Weird."

374
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:48,160
Seriously. I want to ride a horse dressed like this.

375
00:14:50,190 --> 00:14:52,960
We are meeting for the first time.

376
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:54,300
What should we call each other?

377
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:55,730
I'll call you like brothers.

378
00:14:55,730 --> 00:14:56,730
Big brother, second brother.

379
00:14:56,730 --> 00:14:58,100
- Big brother, second brother.
- Yes.

380
00:14:58,100 --> 00:15:00,670
Just speak casually to us.

381
00:15:01,010 --> 00:15:02,340
- Please do.
- Is that okay?

382
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:03,440
- That's fine.
- Really?

383
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:05,380
I really don't like formal speech.

384
00:15:05,380 --> 00:15:08,310
Same. Hyun Moo isn't pretending. He's serious.

385
00:15:08,310 --> 00:15:10,950
Being treated so formally is...

386
00:15:10,950 --> 00:15:12,420
It limits how close we can get.

387
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:14,290
Right. You're right.

388
00:15:14,290 --> 00:15:16,220
Do you like to travel?

389
00:15:16,220 --> 00:15:18,120
Yes, I love to travel.

390
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:19,720
Speaking formally right after saying you won't.

391
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:21,290
Oh, should I start speaking casually now?

392
00:15:21,290 --> 00:15:22,490
Start.

393
00:15:22,830 --> 00:15:24,330
- Do you like to travel?
- I love it.

394
00:15:24,330 --> 00:15:25,460
So much.

395
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:27,700
I always travel whenever I have the time.

396
00:15:27,700 --> 00:15:29,370
- We're the same.
- Yes.

397
00:15:29,630 --> 00:15:32,400
Do you plan your trips in advance?

398
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:33,640
I'm totally spontaneous.

399
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:35,510
Spontaneous? Oh, nice.

400
00:15:35,510 --> 00:15:36,710
- We're similar.
- Nice.

401
00:15:36,710 --> 00:15:38,740
Even with flights and hotels,

402
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:40,880
if I'm going to another location, I book it there.

403
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:43,710
- We're the same.
- You're just like Hyun Moo.

404
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:45,250
- Oh, my.
- You're very easygoing.

405
00:15:45,450 --> 00:15:46,650
The important thing...

406
00:15:46,850 --> 00:15:49,290
is that I love to wander around.

407
00:15:49,290 --> 00:15:51,820
So I don't need a very nice hotel.

408
00:15:51,820 --> 00:15:53,360
It feels like kind of a waste.

409
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:54,830
You're female Jun Hyun Moo.

410
00:15:55,090 --> 00:15:56,230
You're female Jun Hyun Moo.

411
00:15:56,490 --> 00:16:00,260
To give you an explanation about this trip...

412
00:16:01,170 --> 00:16:03,970
- You can do whatever you want.
- I love it.

413
00:16:03,970 --> 00:16:05,440
- Seriously.
- Even though we have...

414
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:07,370
some plans to shoot this or that,

415
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:10,970
if we suggest something new, we reflect that right away.

416
00:16:11,310 --> 00:16:12,980
I love that, seriously.

417
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:15,110
Let's say I want to do this,

418
00:16:15,110 --> 00:16:16,510
and you ask to do this.

419
00:16:16,510 --> 00:16:19,220
Alright, you guys, I have some food here for you.

420
00:16:19,220 --> 00:16:20,480
This big old platter right here.

421
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:21,920
- I'll pop it in the middle for you.
- That looks delicious.

422
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:24,320
- This is the platter.
- You have oysters on the side here.

423
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:25,520
Horseradish, some lemon,

424
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:27,890
and this is the house-made passion fruit hot sauce.

425
00:16:27,890 --> 00:16:29,330
We made it in-house here.

426
00:16:29,330 --> 00:16:30,360
- Okay.
- Smoked mussels.

427
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:32,860
I got some salmon crudo with capers and lemon.

428
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:36,270
The ahi with some tomato relish and caperberries as well.

429
00:16:36,270 --> 00:16:38,140
With some chilli and mint for you guys.

430
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:39,140
You guys enjoy it.

431
00:16:39,140 --> 00:16:40,600
- Thank you. Oh, my.
- Oh, my.

432
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:41,740
That looks delicious.

433
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:42,970
(Seafood platter, the fresh taste of the sea in Calgary)

434
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:45,640
To continue what I was saying before...

435
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:47,980
- I got one more here for you guys.
- Okay.

436
00:16:49,410 --> 00:16:50,980
Calamari here. There's some sweet onions,

437
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:52,520
and then a garlic aioli on the side here.

438
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:53,750
I ordered calamari.

439
00:16:54,490 --> 00:16:58,060
More than the disappointment of not getting to do this thing,

440
00:16:58,460 --> 00:17:00,360
- I dislike conflict.
- Right.

441
00:17:00,360 --> 00:17:01,890
It's better to do this, right?

442
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:03,390
I really like that too.

443
00:17:03,590 --> 00:17:06,730
It's better to do what we each want and be happy.

444
00:17:06,730 --> 00:17:09,130
If we're compromising and having to be too mindful,

445
00:17:09,130 --> 00:17:10,870
- we'll slowly get frustrated.
- Of course.

446
00:17:10,870 --> 00:17:12,440
We shouldn't be considerate of each other.

447
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:13,840
Let's have a drink. Being considerate is pointless.

448
00:17:13,840 --> 00:17:15,470
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

449
00:17:15,470 --> 00:17:18,010
(Cheers to a happy trip without being considerate.)

450
00:17:19,210 --> 00:17:20,880
Oh, the oyster is insane.

451
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:22,280
It looks so delicious.

452
00:17:28,590 --> 00:17:31,090
(Oh, my!)

453
00:17:37,330 --> 00:17:39,500
(Fried calamari)

454
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:46,340
Oh, Hyun Moo. This is delicious.

455
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:48,340
- The calamari?
- Yes, it's so good.

456
00:18:00,620 --> 00:18:01,690
What did you do today?

457
00:18:01,690 --> 00:18:04,150
Today... I was still jet lagged.

458
00:18:04,990 --> 00:18:07,290
I fell asleep at 12 and woke up at 5.

459
00:18:07,690 --> 00:18:09,560
So I was wondering what to do.

460
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:11,760
I like wandering around by myself.

461
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:15,730
So I took a train that connects the outskirts to the center...

462
00:18:16,270 --> 00:18:18,640
and went to a neighbourhood called Sunnyside.

463
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,170
(Ju Bin headed to Sunnyside, 15 minutes from Stephen Avenue.)

464
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,670
(If Stephen Avenue is Myeongdong,)

465
00:18:21,670 --> 00:18:22,870
(Sunnyside feels like Seoul's Seongsu-dong.)

466
00:18:23,470 --> 00:18:25,210
I checked out some small shops,

467
00:18:25,210 --> 00:18:26,580
- went to a cafe...
- That sounds so nice.

468
00:18:26,580 --> 00:18:28,110
You had a good time.

469
00:18:28,110 --> 00:18:29,510
- Totally.
- You travel well by yourself.

470
00:18:32,850 --> 00:18:35,220
I have a question. Did you search things,

471
00:18:35,220 --> 00:18:36,420
or did you just walk around?

472
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:37,990
I just went. I just got on.

473
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:41,390
I saw that the train would take me to downtown,

474
00:18:41,390 --> 00:18:42,690
and I searched from there.

475
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:45,800
She might be the best travel buddy we've had so far.

476
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:46,800
Seriously.

477
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:48,330
- Just going anywhere.
- Exactly.

478
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,030
Here.

479
00:18:51,030 --> 00:18:52,700
(Calabrian salami pizza, the strong and spicy aroma of salami)

480
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:54,300
Let's dig in.

481
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:55,910
- Let's eat. Shall we?
- Let's go.

482
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:13,360
(What is this flavour?)

483
00:19:15,130 --> 00:19:16,960
- What is this?
- Isn't it good?

484
00:19:17,530 --> 00:19:19,130
It's totally different from how it looks.

485
00:19:19,230 --> 00:19:21,200
- It didn't look that amazing.
- It's good, right?

486
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:22,800
It's so good.

487
00:19:23,170 --> 00:19:24,470
- It really is good.
- It's so good.

488
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:28,940
I love this.

489
00:19:29,110 --> 00:19:30,970
(They've fallen in love...)

490
00:19:30,970 --> 00:19:34,750
(with the rich taste of salami pizza.)

491
00:19:35,650 --> 00:19:36,650
(Campanelle pasta)

492
00:19:46,590 --> 00:19:47,890
Why is this so good?

493
00:19:48,890 --> 00:19:50,430
Memorize the name. Campanella.

494
00:19:50,430 --> 00:19:52,460
- Panpan?
- Campanella.

495
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:53,630
- Campanella?
- Campanella?

496
00:19:54,330 --> 00:19:57,070
This is kind of like sujebi.

497
00:19:57,070 --> 00:19:58,100
I'm curious.

498
00:20:03,140 --> 00:20:05,310
The texture is so fun.

499
00:20:06,410 --> 00:20:07,680
It's kind of like sujebi.

500
00:20:08,210 --> 00:20:10,080
- I like sujebi.
- It's good.

501
00:20:10,580 --> 00:20:12,320
It's just the first meal, and I think...

502
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:14,750
I've found my favourite restaurant ever.

503
00:20:14,750 --> 00:20:18,260
(The Canada trip is off to a good start.)

504
00:20:18,690 --> 00:20:20,620
- Do you want this?
- I'm okay.

505
00:20:21,630 --> 00:20:23,160
- Do you want this?
- Go ahead.

506
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:24,530
Go ahead.

507
00:20:24,530 --> 00:20:25,900
(If you insist.)

508
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:28,300
This place was so good.

509
00:20:29,070 --> 00:20:30,900
I like it.

510
00:20:31,740 --> 00:20:33,900
(Friendship between our three travel buddies...)

511
00:20:33,900 --> 00:20:36,340
(has started to bloom on this night in Calgary.)

512
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:39,680
Oh, I'm full.

513
00:20:39,680 --> 00:20:41,610
- Thank you for the meal.
- Thank you for the meal.

514
00:20:42,250 --> 00:20:43,310
Let's go.

515
00:20:44,950 --> 00:20:45,980
Do you not get your hair and makeup done?

516
00:20:45,980 --> 00:20:46,980
No, I don't.

517
00:20:47,150 --> 00:20:48,450
- Really?
- Joon doesn't.

518
00:20:49,390 --> 00:20:50,590
- Oh, my.
- He doesn't bring clothes either.

519
00:20:50,590 --> 00:20:51,960
He wore the same outfit for four days.

520
00:20:52,090 --> 00:20:53,220
That's a bit...

521
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:55,290
- But here's the thing...
- You should've bought some there.

522
00:20:55,290 --> 00:20:56,360
That's a bit...

523
00:20:56,360 --> 00:20:58,500
I have to explain myself to every guest about this.

524
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:00,630
Goodness. Hear me out.

525
00:21:00,630 --> 00:21:02,830
I'm famous for not having body odour.

526
00:21:02,830 --> 00:21:04,200
Oh, my. Really?

527
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:07,370
- Which of the two are better?
- Right.

528
00:21:16,510 --> 00:21:17,880
