00:43:45,560 --> 00:43:47,830
- Look at those berries.
- Berries.

1051
00:43:47,960 --> 00:43:49,330
It's an actual Western pear.

1052
00:43:49,570 --> 00:43:52,370
They must have little craft items too.

1053
00:43:54,500 --> 00:43:56,340
They're so cute and adorable.

1054
00:43:57,240 --> 00:43:59,410
Do you normally look for food or little items...

1055
00:43:59,410 --> 00:44:01,380
- when you come to a market?
- Little items.

1056
00:44:01,380 --> 00:44:02,540
- Really?
- Yes.

1057
00:44:03,110 --> 00:44:04,280
There's food!

1058
00:44:05,050 --> 00:44:06,780
- Coffee and donuts.
- Can we eat first?

1059
00:44:06,980 --> 00:44:08,080
Let's go.

1060
00:44:09,350 --> 00:44:10,420
That's so cute.

1061
00:44:12,620 --> 00:44:14,160
- It's adorable!
- Who made these?

1062
00:44:14,360 --> 00:44:15,590
I've never seen anything like it.

1063
00:44:17,060 --> 00:44:18,490
It's cooked and flipped over. Look.

1064
00:44:19,090 --> 00:44:20,300
- That's so cute.
- So cute!

1065
00:44:22,000 --> 00:44:23,230
It's sugar.

1066
00:44:24,630 --> 00:44:25,830
Thank you.

1067
00:44:26,270 --> 00:44:27,400
- Okay.
- Okay.

1068
00:44:27,400 --> 00:44:28,470
Thank you.

1069
00:44:29,070 --> 00:44:30,270
- Thank you so much.
- Okay.

1070
00:44:30,270 --> 00:44:31,340
It smells delicious.

1071
00:44:31,340 --> 00:44:32,780
- We need coffee for this.
- We do.

1072
00:44:32,780 --> 00:44:34,480
(He puts it straight into his mouth.)

1073
00:44:37,810 --> 00:44:38,910
It's good.

1074
00:44:40,280 --> 00:44:41,850
Coffee looks good.

1075
00:44:42,680 --> 00:44:44,790
(I'm feeling iced Americano today.)

1076
00:44:45,720 --> 00:44:47,590
(Resting with donuts and iced coffee)

1077
00:44:47,590 --> 00:44:49,690
- it's good.
- Is it?

1078
00:44:49,690 --> 00:44:51,760
- It's really good.
- That looks tasty.

1079
00:44:57,500 --> 00:44:59,200
Even the dogs look happy.

1080
00:45:03,840 --> 00:45:05,610
It's so nice and peaceful.

1081
00:45:08,580 --> 00:45:10,280
Look at that dog sitting!

1082
00:45:10,980 --> 00:45:12,650
- That's adorable.
- That's a person.

1083
00:45:14,150 --> 00:45:15,250
He's begging.

1084
00:45:15,250 --> 00:45:16,290
(Salivating)

1085
00:45:16,290 --> 00:45:17,450
She's so cute.

1086
00:45:17,650 --> 00:45:18,920
(Give me some too.)

1087
00:45:18,920 --> 00:45:20,260
No, you're not supposed to eat it.

1088
00:45:20,760 --> 00:45:22,060
Hi.

1089
00:45:22,690 --> 00:45:24,390
She must like people.

1090
00:45:24,560 --> 00:45:25,830
Good girl.

1091
00:45:26,560 --> 00:45:28,060
Stop.

1092
00:45:29,030 --> 00:45:31,730
She's not even motivated to do stuff like that,

1093
00:45:31,730 --> 00:45:34,240
but she can't turn down a treat, so...

1094
00:45:35,300 --> 00:45:37,570
- They have this dog treat...
- Oh, no!

1095
00:45:37,710 --> 00:45:38,770
Junie!

1096
00:45:39,110 --> 00:45:40,680
- Bad dog.
- Oh, yes.

1097
00:45:41,380 --> 00:45:42,540
No.

1098
00:45:42,540 --> 00:45:45,080
So tempting.

1099
00:45:46,320 --> 00:45:47,850
- Thank you.
- Bye.

1100
00:45:48,380 --> 00:45:49,720
That was comforting.

1101
00:45:50,290 --> 00:45:51,850
(The scenery makes every moment comforting.)

1102
00:45:51,850 --> 00:45:52,990
It's so comforting.

1103
00:45:54,060 --> 00:45:56,460
- I love it.
- The air is amazing.

1104
00:45:57,130 --> 00:46:00,160
It's been so long since I last smelled this air.

1105
00:46:00,160 --> 00:46:01,860
This fresh air.

1106
00:46:02,930 --> 00:46:04,500
Oh, my gosh.

1107
00:46:04,970 --> 00:46:06,740
- It's a duck!
- Where?

1108
00:46:07,200 --> 00:46:08,400
Is it a Canada goose?

1109
00:46:11,670 --> 00:46:14,380
Even this feels good. This...

1110
00:46:15,640 --> 00:46:17,050
This place is lovely.

1111
00:46:20,850 --> 00:46:22,420
- Big Head Town.
- Welcome to the Big Head.

1112
00:46:25,120 --> 00:46:27,120
I never knew how beautiful Canmore was.

1113
00:46:27,120 --> 00:46:28,120
Nice.

1114
00:46:29,190 --> 00:46:31,090
It's so nice and pretty.

1115
00:46:32,090 --> 00:46:34,830
- Look at that.
- That's incredible.

1116
00:46:35,660 --> 00:46:38,200
- Look at that.
- That's incredible.

1117
00:46:39,030 --> 00:46:40,270
This looks amazing!

1118
00:46:40,270 --> 00:46:41,340
(This looks amazing!)

1119
00:46:41,970 --> 00:46:44,370
Right? No matter where you look, it's magnificent.

1120
00:46:44,370 --> 00:46:45,970
- It's gorgeous.
- Everywhere you look,

1121
00:46:45,970 --> 00:46:48,440
- it's beautiful.
- It's like a painting.

1122
00:46:48,440 --> 00:46:49,950
(Canmore is picture-perfect, whichever way you turn.)

1123
00:46:49,950 --> 00:46:51,150
That's like a photo.

1124
00:46:52,150 --> 00:46:54,150
I must take a photo of this view.

1125
00:46:54,150 --> 00:46:58,150
Hyun Moo, stand in the middle. I'll take photos of you.

1126
00:46:58,420 --> 00:47:00,490
(He runs into the painting to capture this moment.)

1127
00:47:00,490 --> 00:47:02,960
- Stop. Too far.
- You're too far.

1128
00:47:03,090 --> 00:47:04,830
I know it's old-fashioned, but count to three for me.

1129
00:47:04,960 --> 00:47:06,530
One, two, three!

1130
00:47:06,730 --> 00:47:08,230
Does it look like I can jump high?

1131
00:47:08,860 --> 00:47:11,600
(The giant mountain peak in the palm of my hand)

1132
00:47:11,970 --> 00:47:13,570
I'm taking it.

1133
00:47:13,840 --> 00:47:15,100
Why are you walking toward me?

1134
00:47:16,170 --> 00:47:17,510
It looks like a traditional outfit.

1135
00:47:17,510 --> 00:47:19,680
(A man of taste for the arts)

1136
00:47:20,140 --> 00:47:21,280
- Oh, that's it.
- Here?

1137
00:47:21,280 --> 00:47:23,010
Come forward.

1138
00:47:26,250 --> 00:47:27,420
- Good.
- That's a good photo.

1139
00:47:27,420 --> 00:47:28,580
You look so tall.

1140
00:47:28,580 --> 00:47:30,190
(An actress's insane proportions)

1141
00:47:30,720 --> 00:47:31,820
It's modern art.

1142
00:47:31,990 --> 00:47:33,260
Performance art.

1143
00:47:33,260 --> 00:47:35,360
You have to dance to "Catch Catch" to make it performance art.

1144
00:47:35,960 --> 00:47:37,160
It's modern art.

1145
00:47:37,160 --> 00:47:39,260
(The lucky duo at the Rocky Mountains)

1146
00:47:40,060 --> 00:47:41,560
Of all the countries I've been to,

1147
00:47:41,560 --> 00:47:44,100
this is the most peaceful.

1148
00:47:45,230 --> 00:47:48,940
(There's peace on every street of Canmore.)

1149
00:47:50,870 --> 00:47:52,640
I'm craving more food, though.

1150
00:47:52,640 --> 00:47:53,710
You can eat more.

1151
00:47:54,110 --> 00:47:55,280
Should we check this one out?

1152
00:47:55,910 --> 00:47:57,180
It looks like a good place.

1153
00:47:57,310 --> 00:47:59,550
- That's a famous one.
- Is it?

1154
00:47:59,720 --> 00:48:00,950
"BeaverTails."

1155
00:48:01,080 --> 00:48:02,080
"BeaverTails?"

1156
00:48:02,080 --> 00:48:04,120
- Beaver's tail.
- A beaver's tail?

1157
00:48:04,590 --> 00:48:05,950
The donuts are shaped like beavers' tails.

1158
00:48:06,260 --> 00:48:07,560
- Oh, donuts?
- Donuts?

1159
00:48:08,420 --> 00:48:10,290
- Let's check it out.
- I've seen it before.

1160
00:48:10,630 --> 00:48:11,960
BeaverTails.

1161
00:48:13,130 --> 00:48:14,230
- Hello.
- Hello.

1162
00:48:14,800 --> 00:48:17,000
(They flatten the rounded dough...)

1163
00:48:17,000 --> 00:48:20,300
(and plunge it into the oil.)

1164
00:48:20,940 --> 00:48:24,910
(A flat shape that looks like a beaver's tail)

1165
00:48:27,510 --> 00:48:30,580
(Add various toppings to your liking, and it's good to go.)

1166
00:48:30,780 --> 00:48:32,350
- Thank you for the food.
- Just eat it like this?

1167
00:48:32,350 --> 00:48:33,820
- Yes.
- It looks like pizza.

1168
00:48:34,180 --> 00:48:36,850
But it tastes totally different. It's so sweet.

1169
00:48:36,850 --> 00:48:38,390
(The donuts look like pizza. How will they taste?)

1170
00:48:42,920 --> 00:48:44,360
It's so good.

1171
00:48:44,360 --> 00:48:46,230
- Is it that good?
- Yes, it's amazing.

1172
00:48:46,430 --> 00:48:48,200
(This looks interesting.)

1173
00:48:53,370 --> 00:48:54,740
It can't taste bad.

1174
00:48:55,640 --> 00:48:56,940
Is this avocado?

1175
00:48:58,470 --> 00:48:59,680
Oh, this is...

1176
00:49:01,180 --> 00:49:02,310
That's new.

1177
00:49:03,180 --> 00:49:06,150
- The dough is a bit like...
- Danish pastry.

1178
00:49:06,150 --> 00:49:07,220
Yes, pastry.

1179
00:49:07,420 --> 00:49:09,420
- I like how thin it is.
- Yes.

1180
00:49:09,420 --> 00:49:10,750
I can eat it more cleanly.

1181
00:49:11,290 --> 00:49:12,750
- This is so good.
- Right.

1182
00:49:12,750 --> 00:49:14,620
It's so good that I feel like I could die.

1183
00:49:14,660 --> 00:49:15,790
This is good.

1184
00:49:16,190 --> 00:49:18,330
- Here, Ju Bin.
- Thanks.

1185
00:49:19,130 --> 00:49:20,930
- Joon, try this.
- What's this?

1186
00:49:21,130 --> 00:49:22,560
It's called the Avalanche.

1187
00:49:22,860 --> 00:49:24,170
- It's a snow slide.
- Like a snow slide?

1188
00:49:25,030 --> 00:49:26,470
It's got chocolate and stuff.

1189
00:49:29,470 --> 00:49:30,640
- It's good.
- Right?

1190
00:49:30,640 --> 00:49:31,670
Yes.

1191
00:49:33,480 --> 00:49:35,640
(They leisurely enjoy their sweets.)

1192
00:49:35,640 --> 00:49:36,850
I can't stop eating it.

1193
00:49:37,610 --> 00:49:40,120
Are we just hanging out like this without a plan?

1194
00:49:41,250 --> 00:49:42,350
That's what a trip is.

1195
00:49:42,350 --> 00:49:44,350
- This is too real.
- I love it.

1196
00:49:45,220 --> 00:49:46,320
The leisure.

1197
00:49:47,290 --> 00:49:49,160
Should we spend some time separately?

1198
00:49:49,160 --> 00:49:50,230
Thirty minutes?

1199
00:49:50,590 --> 00:49:52,030
- See you.
- Have fun.

1200
00:49:55,430 --> 00:49:56,430
(Sighing)

1201
00:49:56,430 --> 00:49:57,470
This is nice.

1202
00:50:01,140 --> 00:50:02,370
Wouldn't that be worth watching?

1203
00:50:02,370 --> 00:50:03,710
Alberta...

1204
00:50:04,240 --> 00:50:07,410
(Hyun Moo wants to shop and enters a store.)

1205
00:50:09,240 --> 00:50:11,880
Good dog.

1206
00:50:12,410 --> 00:50:13,520
You're lazy.

1207
00:50:13,520 --> 00:50:14,880
(Instead, he begins rubbing a dog's belly.)

1208
00:50:14,880 --> 00:50:15,950
Thank you.

1209
00:50:15,950 --> 00:50:17,550
(He exits after only looking at a dog.)

1210
00:50:23,130 --> 00:50:24,590
This place makes me calm.

1211
00:50:25,330 --> 00:50:26,630
There are mountains back and forth.

1212
00:50:30,900 --> 00:50:33,970
(Humming)

1213
00:50:34,240 --> 00:50:37,670
(Humming)

1214
00:50:40,980 --> 00:50:42,510
(Oh, my)

1215
00:50:42,910 --> 00:50:43,980
Hello.

1216
00:50:43,980 --> 00:50:45,480
(She found a dog that picked up something amazing.)

1217
00:50:45,710 --> 00:50:47,750
- Excuse me, sir.
- Sure.

1218
00:50:47,750 --> 00:50:48,820
Could I pet your... Okay.

1219
00:50:48,820 --> 00:50:50,250
Everybody else does it.

1220
00:50:51,150 --> 00:50:52,250
Thank you.

1221
00:50:53,560 --> 00:50:54,690
(Touch me.)

1222
00:50:54,690 --> 00:50:56,360
So cute!

1223
00:51:01,230 --> 00:51:02,300
How adorable.

1224
00:51:02,430 --> 00:51:04,230
It must have taken a shower. The hair's all wet.

1225
00:51:04,430 --> 00:51:06,500
Do you want me to go? Bye.

1226
00:51:06,900 --> 00:51:08,840
Bite it again.

1227
00:51:11,210 --> 00:51:13,940
Come on. Bring that with you. We're going home.

1228
00:51:14,480 --> 00:51:15,580
Thank you.

1229
00:51:16,280 --> 00:51:17,980
Thank you so much.

1230
00:51:19,510 --> 00:51:20,720
How adorable!

1231
00:51:21,520 --> 00:51:22,750
I should have handed over the center.

1232
00:51:23,220 --> 00:51:24,320
It must be tiring.

1233
00:51:28,360 --> 00:51:29,560
I'll just have to look around.

1234
00:51:31,360 --> 00:51:34,630
(Joon meanderingly wanders the small town.)

1235
00:51:37,700 --> 00:51:39,300
(And he enters when a store catches his eyes.)

1236
00:51:39,300 --> 00:51:41,070
All the shops look amazing.

1237
00:51:42,170 --> 00:51:43,540
They have cute clothes.

1238
00:51:44,740 --> 00:51:46,140
Isn't this hoodie so cute?

1239
00:51:47,540 --> 00:51:50,380
(After choosing the outfit, he gets changed into it.)

1240
00:51:50,380 --> 00:51:51,550
It's so nice.

1241
00:51:51,550 --> 00:51:53,420
(And he walks straight to the counter.)

1242
00:51:54,150 --> 00:51:56,050
Can I pay like this?

1243
00:51:57,490 --> 00:51:58,550
- Yes.
- Thank you.

1244
00:51:59,020 --> 00:52:01,520
I might wear this like a uniform.

1245
00:52:02,120 --> 00:52:03,260
I love it so much.

1246
00:52:05,630 --> 00:52:08,600
It's cold out. This is perfect.

1247
00:52:09,560 --> 00:52:10,970
I love it! What do I do?

1248
00:52:11,470 --> 00:52:14,140
(A cool breeze blows across the icy glaciers)

1249
00:52:14,440 --> 00:52:17,370
(Even Canada's breeze is refreshing.)

1250
00:52:18,510 --> 00:52:19,810
You bought something?

1251
00:52:20,280 --> 00:52:21,640
You actually bought something?

1252
00:52:21,810 --> 00:52:24,410
- Isn't it pretty? I had to buy it.
- It is.

1253
00:52:24,410 --> 00:52:25,910
- Did you buy anything?
- I did.

1254
00:52:25,910 --> 00:52:27,150
- What did you get?
- What did you get?

1255
00:52:28,750 --> 00:52:29,850
What colours do you like?

1256
00:52:31,090 --> 00:52:32,250
Yellow and green.

1257
00:52:32,250 --> 00:52:33,590
Yellow and green?

1258
00:52:34,390 --> 00:52:36,290
- What's that?
- My gosh, you got a T-shirt?

1259
00:52:36,390 --> 00:52:38,330
- My gosh, it's nice.
- The fabric felt really nice.

1260
00:52:38,890 --> 00:52:40,430
Joon would wear an XL, right?

1261
00:52:40,960 --> 00:52:42,060
Alberta.

1262
00:52:42,430 --> 00:52:44,200
I don't know women's sizes, but is XS standard?

1263
00:52:46,840 --> 00:52:48,100
Can a person even fit into this?

1264
00:52:48,800 --> 00:52:50,240
Oh, it's my size.

1265
00:52:50,910 --> 00:52:52,370
- Oh, it's my size.
- What colour did you say you liked?

1266
00:52:52,470 --> 00:52:53,910
- Blue.
- Blue?

1267
00:52:53,910 --> 00:52:54,940
- Yes.
- That's amazing.

1268
00:52:55,710 --> 00:52:56,750
My gosh!

1269
00:52:56,910 --> 00:52:58,580
- I'm Choi Hyun Woo.
- But that's the T-shirt!

1270
00:52:58,580 --> 00:53:00,120
- What is this?
- I'm a magician.

1271
00:53:00,120 --> 00:53:02,980
- How did you do that?
- You don't have 30 shirts in there?

1272
00:53:02,980 --> 00:53:04,490
- Could I fit 30 in here?
- Hyun Moo.

1273
00:53:04,990 --> 00:53:07,720
All right, everyone. It's my turn to impress you.

1274
00:53:08,890 --> 00:53:10,790
What? Really?

1275
00:53:10,960 --> 00:53:12,130
It's bigger than mine.

1276
00:53:12,960 --> 00:53:14,030
For all three of us?

1277
00:53:14,260 --> 00:53:16,870
- The same one.
- My gosh!

1278
00:53:17,170 --> 00:53:19,170
- My gosh, thank you.
- Matching T-shirts.

1279
00:53:19,170 --> 00:53:20,800
- Really? All three match.
- Yes.

1280
00:53:21,170 --> 00:53:23,170
I said I hate T-shirts with place names on them.

1281
00:53:24,370 --> 00:53:25,510
But I like free stuff.

1282
00:53:25,640 --> 00:53:26,880
It's nice, though.

1283
00:53:26,880 --> 00:53:28,510
It has that college student look.

1284
00:53:28,680 --> 00:53:30,550
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

1285
00:53:31,980 --> 00:53:34,050
- It's getting a little chilly.
- The wind's picking up.

1286
00:53:35,120 --> 00:53:37,190
The weather's changed so much since earlier.

1287
00:53:38,620 --> 00:53:39,990
What shall we do now?

1288
00:53:40,090 --> 00:53:42,860
- Let's enjoy Canmore's nature.
- What are we doing now?

1289
00:53:42,960 --> 00:53:45,430
- Yes.
- Most people climb a mountain...

1290
00:53:45,630 --> 00:53:48,060
and look down from the summit.

1291
00:53:48,500 --> 00:53:49,730
But there's another way.

1292
00:53:50,270 --> 00:53:52,730
You can look up from below.

1293
00:53:52,830 --> 00:53:55,240
Just look up from right here.

1294
00:53:56,140 --> 00:53:57,870
Is there a monorail or something?

1295
00:53:57,870 --> 00:53:59,410
- I don't think they have one.
- A monorail.

1296
00:53:59,410 --> 00:54:00,410
VR?

1297
00:54:00,410 --> 00:54:02,080
- VR?
- It's VR.

1298
00:54:02,080 --> 00:54:03,580
We came all this way for VR?

1299
00:54:03,980 --> 00:54:05,550
- Oh!
- Are we riding something?

1300
00:54:05,550 --> 00:54:06,620
What is it?

1301
00:54:06,620 --> 00:54:09,820
- There are lakes around here.
- Yes.

1302
00:54:09,990 --> 00:54:12,720
- I think we'll take a boat ride.
- Oh, really?

1303
00:54:12,820 --> 00:54:14,890
- Correct! A boat!
- Really?

1304
00:54:15,720 --> 00:54:18,230
So we'll go right into the scenery.

1305
00:54:18,230 --> 00:54:20,460
- It's so beautiful.
- Look to your right.

1306
00:54:20,460 --> 00:54:21,830
- My gosh, look at that water!
- My gosh!

1307
00:54:22,030 --> 00:54:23,700
- My gosh!
- My gosh!

1308
00:54:23,700 --> 00:54:25,770
My gosh, look at that water colour!

1309
00:54:25,970 --> 00:54:27,240
- My gosh!
- My gosh!

1310
00:54:27,240 --> 00:54:28,700
That's insane.

1311
00:54:28,700 --> 00:54:29,970
That's crazy.

1312
00:54:29,970 --> 00:54:30,970
My gosh!

1313
00:54:36,750 --> 00:54:39,210
My gosh, that water colour is unreal.

1314
00:54:41,250 --> 00:54:44,550
Goodness. A place like this exists?

1315
00:54:45,290 --> 00:54:46,620
Isn't that an unusual water colour?

1316
00:54:46,620 --> 00:54:48,390
It's the colour of a sports drink.

1317
00:54:48,390 --> 00:54:50,060
- Emerald.
- They mixed it with energy drink.

1318
00:54:51,660 --> 00:54:52,760
The reason is...

1319
00:54:52,760 --> 00:54:55,460
it's glacial meltwater that gives it this colour.

1320
00:54:55,460 --> 00:54:57,770
- Oh, really?
- As the glaciers melt,

1321
00:54:58,030 --> 00:54:59,300
they grind down the rocks...

1322
00:54:59,930 --> 00:55:01,240
which gives the water this colour.

1323
00:55:01,970 --> 00:55:04,940
Older folks would call it jade green.

1324
00:55:08,880 --> 00:55:10,410
My gosh, it's so beautiful here.

1325
00:55:11,080 --> 00:55:12,910
My goodness, look at this.

1326
00:55:12,910 --> 00:55:15,320
- Are we riding that rubber boat?
- That's the one.

1327
00:55:15,320 --> 00:55:16,480
Let's go!

1328
00:55:16,480 --> 00:55:18,390
(Become part of a postcard scene while rafting on the Bow River)

1329
00:55:23,460 --> 00:55:24,830
- Are you guys on the boat?
- Yes.

1330
00:55:24,830 --> 00:55:26,430
- Perfect.
- Thank you.

1331
00:55:26,430 --> 00:55:28,700
So these are universal.

1332
00:55:29,430 --> 00:55:30,770
- Thank you.
- Here we are.

1333
00:55:30,770 --> 00:55:32,030
(They put on the life jacket.)

1334
00:55:32,030 --> 00:55:34,500
You sit down and spin your legs around.

1335
00:55:34,870 --> 00:55:37,570
Turn around and we're just going to sit on the orange tubes here.

1336
00:55:37,710 --> 00:55:38,970
- Cool.
- Are we good?

1337
00:55:38,970 --> 00:55:40,810
- Yes.
- Awesome. Let's get on it.

1338
00:55:42,780 --> 00:55:44,280
Goodness.

1339
00:55:45,210 --> 00:55:46,510
Gosh.

1340
00:55:46,510 --> 00:55:47,580
Did she say to sit here like this?

1341
00:55:47,580 --> 00:55:49,020
- Ju Bin, sit in the middle.
- Okay.

1342
00:55:49,880 --> 00:55:51,050
Goodness.

1343
00:55:51,790 --> 00:55:53,390
This is kind of scary.

1344
00:55:53,390 --> 00:55:55,690
Lean back for a second, and it's all over.

1345
00:55:56,360 --> 00:55:58,030
There's nothing to hold on to.

1346
00:55:58,560 --> 00:56:00,960
If I feel like I'm falling, I'll grab on to you.

1347
00:56:00,960 --> 00:56:02,500
So you want us to die together?

1348
00:56:03,470 --> 00:56:04,570
Okay.

1349
00:56:04,770 --> 00:56:05,830
Here we go.

1350
00:56:05,830 --> 00:56:08,240
Oh, this is scary.

1351
00:56:10,000 --> 00:56:13,340
(Nervous Joon can't sit still.)

1352
00:56:13,540 --> 00:56:15,980
You can hardly call this rafting.

1353
00:56:16,680 --> 00:56:20,850
(The river is so calm, his nerves seem silly now)

1354
00:56:36,330 --> 00:56:38,130
Welcome out to the Bow River.

1355
00:56:38,130 --> 00:56:40,070
My name is Remy. I'll be with you guys.

1356
00:56:40,240 --> 00:56:41,870
(Take good care of us!)

1357
00:56:42,240 --> 00:56:45,140
(Today's rafting route for the trio)

1358
00:56:45,570 --> 00:56:46,670
My goodness.

1359
00:56:46,670 --> 00:56:49,880
(An 8km route along the jade-green river)

1360
00:56:52,780 --> 00:56:55,150
Do you know the three peaks right behind me?

1361
00:56:56,150 --> 00:56:57,290
Do you know their names?

1362
00:56:57,290 --> 00:56:58,520
- No.
- Three Sisters.

1363
00:56:58,520 --> 00:56:59,720
Three Sisters?

1364
00:56:59,720 --> 00:57:00,860
You guys can stay on the boat.

1365
00:57:00,860 --> 00:57:04,530
So that's why the sign said Three Sisters on the way here.

1366
00:57:04,730 --> 00:57:08,360
(The Three Sisters, an icon of the Rockies)

1367
00:57:08,630 --> 00:57:10,330
So we have Hope at the bottom.

1368
00:57:10,330 --> 00:57:12,800
And Faith, Charity up top.

1369
00:57:13,100 --> 00:57:16,140
Those are the names of them from when they were first discovered.

1370
00:57:16,140 --> 00:57:17,570
Goodness.

1371
00:57:17,740 --> 00:57:19,440
Why sisters, not brothers?

1372
00:57:20,780 --> 00:57:22,580
Actually the part of the reason is...

1373
00:57:22,580 --> 00:57:25,310
The Europeans thought they looked like nuns.

1374
00:57:25,310 --> 00:57:27,050
Because they have all the snow on them...

1375
00:57:27,050 --> 00:57:28,780
and they are wrapped up in a veil.

1376
00:57:29,080 --> 00:57:30,690
So that's why they got that name.

1377
00:57:31,990 --> 00:57:33,150
What do you guys think?

1378
00:57:35,690 --> 00:57:36,830
It's like a painting.

1379
00:57:36,830 --> 00:57:38,760
My gosh, it's like a commercial.

1380
00:57:39,330 --> 00:57:40,460
It's so beautiful.

1381
00:57:40,630 --> 00:57:42,060
Are they capturing us like a painting?

1382
00:57:48,840 --> 00:57:52,270
It's a shame the camera might not do this justice...

1383
00:57:53,810 --> 00:57:55,010
It's unreal.

1384
00:57:56,410 --> 00:57:58,050
I don't know how to describe it.

1385
00:57:58,380 --> 00:58:00,750
I can hardly believe I'm seeing this with my own eyes.

1386
00:58:06,620 --> 00:58:07,760
It's so peaceful.

1387
00:58:09,560 --> 00:58:10,960
It still doesn't feel real.

1388
00:58:19,000 --> 00:58:20,900
Everything's so beautiful, I...

1389
00:58:21,240 --> 00:58:22,370
It's all so beautiful.

1390
00:58:22,840 --> 00:58:25,010
It's like it's just us and nature.

1391
00:58:25,010 --> 00:58:27,080
("It's like it's just us and nature.")

1392
00:58:28,240 --> 00:58:29,880
(Hyun Moo notices...)

1393
00:58:29,880 --> 00:58:33,110
(a loving couple.)

1394
00:58:33,410 --> 00:58:35,320
That couple up front looks lovely, don't they?

1395
00:58:35,320 --> 00:58:36,380
- Yes.
- Yes.

1396
00:58:36,650 --> 00:58:38,850
- They're an elderly couple.
- They seem so close.

1397
00:58:38,850 --> 00:58:40,490
- I know.
- They're so devoted to each other.

1398
00:58:41,020 --> 00:58:42,890
When will that be me?

1399
00:58:52,530 --> 00:58:53,740
That's an eagle.

1400
00:58:54,200 --> 00:58:55,640
- Eagle.
- Crow.

1401
00:58:55,640 --> 00:58:56,700
Oh, it's a crow?

1402
00:58:56,700 --> 00:58:58,610
- How is that an eagle?
- It's so big.

1403
00:58:58,670 --> 00:58:59,710
- It is big.
- Crow.

1404
00:58:59,710 --> 00:59:00,880
Is it eagle?

1405
00:59:00,940 --> 00:59:02,380
- Crow, right?
- Crow.

1406
00:59:02,510 --> 00:59:04,010
What's with this guy?

1407
00:59:04,010 --> 00:59:06,080
Birds in Canada are really big.

1408
00:59:06,080 --> 00:59:07,880
Please only say things like that in Korean.

1409
00:59:08,020 --> 00:59:09,080
They're huge!

1410
00:59:09,080 --> 00:59:10,820
That's a crow? At that size?

1411
00:59:11,620 --> 00:59:13,690
Have you seen any wildlife yet?

1412
00:59:13,860 --> 00:59:14,890
No, not yet.

1413
00:59:15,920 --> 00:59:17,790
- And you guys saw the bear.
- A bear.

1414
00:59:17,790 --> 00:59:19,390
- Yesterday.
- Really?

1415
00:59:19,390 --> 00:59:20,730
Yes, on the road.

1416
00:59:20,730 --> 00:59:21,960
- Where?
- On the road?

1417
00:59:22,100 --> 00:59:23,900
Can I see that?

1418
00:59:23,900 --> 00:59:24,900
Yes.

1419
00:59:24,900 --> 00:59:28,670
Actually, he's eager to see it, the bear.

1420
00:59:30,510 --> 00:59:31,610
I'm curious.

1421
00:59:31,610 --> 00:59:32,810
- I'm too.
- He's curious to see.

1422
00:59:33,140 --> 00:59:34,910
(Here)

1423
00:59:34,910 --> 00:59:36,040
On the road.

1424
00:59:36,040 --> 00:59:39,250
(A wild black bear casually takes over the road.)

1425
00:59:39,610 --> 00:59:41,680
- Goodness.
- My gosh.

1426
00:59:42,820 --> 00:59:44,820
- Weren't you scared?
- We were a little bit scared.

1427
00:59:44,820 --> 00:59:46,390
Not little bit.

1428
00:59:46,390 --> 00:59:47,660
My gosh, this is...

1429
00:59:48,320 --> 00:59:49,590
It's huge.

1430
00:59:50,330 --> 00:59:52,260
A bear can cross the river, right?

1431
00:59:52,390 --> 00:59:54,430
They don't do it a ton, but they will do it.

1432
00:59:54,530 --> 00:59:56,560
(Then...)

1433
00:59:57,000 --> 00:59:59,270
This is mad. This isn't safe.

1434
00:59:59,430 --> 01:00:02,800
We're doing extreme sports.

1435
01:00:03,970 --> 01:00:07,280
A bear can hide inside the forest?

1436
01:00:07,580 --> 01:00:09,840
(Anxious, he mixes 2 languages.)

1437
01:00:10,410 --> 01:00:12,450
Are we shooting "Finding Bear?"

1438
01:00:12,750 --> 01:00:14,480
Just change it to Bear Road.

1439
01:00:14,650 --> 01:00:16,080
Change the title to "This is Bear Road."

1440
01:00:16,080 --> 01:00:17,090
(This is Bear Road)

1441
01:00:24,660 --> 01:00:25,690
Thank you.

1442
01:00:29,460 --> 01:00:31,800
Where's the best photo spot? Here?

1443
01:00:31,800 --> 01:00:35,140
I like that view in the back. I think it's one of the best.

1444
01:00:35,140 --> 01:00:37,740
Or there's also this one.

1445
01:00:37,740 --> 01:00:38,840
They're all good.

1446
01:00:38,940 --> 01:00:40,740
It's nice wherever you go with.

1447
01:00:40,910 --> 01:00:42,880
This side is good, and the view of the Three Sisters is good too.

1448
01:00:43,680 --> 01:00:45,550
It's beautiful everywhere you look.

1449
01:00:49,250 --> 01:00:50,750
This is great too.

1450
01:00:51,990 --> 01:00:54,120
(A photo to treasure for years, framed by dreamlike scenery)

1451
01:00:54,120 --> 01:00:55,560
Yes, I like it.

1452
01:00:58,090 --> 01:00:59,290
We're the three sisters.

1453
01:01:00,860 --> 01:01:02,260
We are three sisters!

1454
01:01:02,660 --> 01:01:03,770
Okay.

1455
01:01:07,570 --> 01:01:09,040
- Thank you very much.
- You're very welcome.

1456
01:01:09,040 --> 01:01:10,240
Thank you.

1457
01:01:16,340 --> 01:01:22,050
(People unwinding in their own way along the Bow River)

1458
01:01:35,930 --> 01:01:37,400
(Snoring)

1459
01:01:39,230 --> 01:01:41,500
(Snoring)

1460
01:01:43,640 --> 01:01:44,970
(Snoring)

1461
01:01:48,280 --> 01:01:51,150
(With Canmore's sky as a blanket...)

1462
01:01:51,150 --> 01:01:54,280
(and the lawn as his bed, Hyun Moo sleeps soundly.)

1463
01:01:55,750 --> 01:01:59,290
(All alone)

1464
01:02:00,690 --> 01:02:04,760
(The rain begins to fall, one drop at a time.)

1465
01:02:06,490 --> 01:02:07,660
Where is he?

1466
01:02:09,700 --> 01:02:10,800
Is that a person?

1467
01:02:10,800 --> 01:02:11,870
He's lying down.

1468
01:02:11,870 --> 01:02:13,870
What? How is he lying down?

1469
01:02:13,870 --> 01:02:14,970
Where's his head?

1470
01:02:15,070 --> 01:02:16,170
I see his feet.

1471
01:02:16,170 --> 01:02:18,670
Let's keep quiet. Let's hurry.

1472
01:02:18,670 --> 01:02:19,870
Should we surprise him?

1473
01:02:21,080 --> 01:02:23,080
(Come this way!)

1474
01:02:27,220 --> 01:02:29,180
My gosh!

1475
01:02:30,450 --> 01:02:33,320
- I couldn't tell if it was you.
- Nice reaction.

1476
01:02:33,320 --> 01:02:35,020
- Love the reaction.
- I know.

1477
01:02:35,020 --> 01:02:37,090
Gosh, I fell asleep.

1478
01:02:37,330 --> 01:02:39,330
It's raining, Hyun Moo.

1479
01:02:39,330 --> 01:02:40,760
I thought you were an anteater.

1480
01:02:40,960 --> 01:02:42,930
Let's sit.

1481
01:02:44,170 --> 01:02:45,770
You're oblivious to danger.

1482
01:02:45,770 --> 01:02:47,970
- I know.
- What if a bear comes as you sleep?

1483
01:02:49,040 --> 01:02:51,470
Bear or no bear, I can't be bothered.

1484
01:02:55,780 --> 01:02:57,040
Is it good?

1485
01:02:58,980 --> 01:03:00,450
Chocolate ice cream.

1486
01:03:00,920 --> 01:03:03,020
It says "Frozen" over there.

1487
01:03:04,090 --> 01:03:06,550
(Ice cream and...)

1488
01:03:06,550 --> 01:03:07,920
- Everything, one.
- Bagel.

1489
01:03:07,920 --> 01:03:10,320
- Everything bagel.
- Do you want it toasted?

1490
01:03:10,390 --> 01:03:11,890
This place is really famous.

1491
01:03:11,890 --> 01:03:13,260
- Doesn't it look delicious?
- Yes.

1492
01:03:17,200 --> 01:03:18,470
What are you eating?

1493
01:03:19,530 --> 01:03:21,270
(Yum)

1494
01:03:21,270 --> 01:03:22,800
Good.

1495
01:03:22,800 --> 01:03:23,970
It's good.

1496
01:03:24,940 --> 01:03:27,680
This is good. I don't usually eat bagels.

1497
01:03:27,680 --> 01:03:30,180
- A woman who doesn't eat bagels?
- I don't eat them much.

1498
01:03:30,180 --> 01:03:32,380
- Never met a woman who skips them.
- Really?

1499
01:03:32,380 --> 01:03:33,510
- Really?
- Yes.

1500
01:03:33,510 --> 01:03:35,080
- That's a first.
- I just think, why bother?

1501
01:03:35,350 --> 01:03:36,420
- Why bother?
- Yes.

1502
01:03:36,420 --> 01:03:37,620
- Really?
- Yes.

1503
01:03:37,850 --> 01:03:39,520
I bet Ju Bin likes spicy stir-fried pork.

1504
01:03:39,520 --> 01:03:40,520
Yes.

1505
01:03:41,590 --> 01:03:43,320
- You're such a guy.
- I really love it.

1506
01:03:43,320 --> 01:03:45,130
- You like tonkatsu, right?
- I really do.

1507
01:03:45,130 --> 01:03:46,460
My tonkatsu has to have cheese.

1508
01:03:46,460 --> 01:03:47,660
I love cheese.

1509
01:03:48,130 --> 01:03:49,960
You're just like a high school boy.

1510
01:03:50,300 --> 01:03:51,700
You're an elementary school boy.

1511
01:03:53,630 --> 01:03:55,440
- What about Hyun Moo?
- I'm the homeroom teacher.

1512
01:03:55,440 --> 01:03:57,040
You're more like a dean of discipline.

1513
01:03:57,040 --> 01:03:59,340
But at a girls' school, not a boys' school.

1514
01:03:59,340 --> 01:04:00,580
Oh, really? Why me?

1515
01:04:00,580 --> 01:04:03,540
You have that "Sure, okay" vibe.

1516
01:04:03,680 --> 01:04:05,810
Like a PE teacher who's bad at sports, right?

1517
01:04:08,150 --> 01:04:10,180
(The rain has eased.)

1518
01:04:10,380 --> 01:04:12,490
Lie down here. It's amazing.

1519
01:04:12,520 --> 01:04:13,790
Should I lie down like this?

1520
01:04:17,020 --> 01:04:18,560
Just lie here.

1521
01:04:18,730 --> 01:04:19,960
Feel the freedom.

1522
01:04:25,800 --> 01:04:27,640
It's so peaceful.

1523
01:04:45,120 --> 01:04:50,420
(An afternoon in the park, everyone unwinding in their own way)

1524
01:04:59,830 --> 01:05:03,470
(As sunset colours the landscape,)

1525
01:05:05,140 --> 01:05:08,980
(the city sparkles with lights as night falls.)

1526
01:05:09,380 --> 01:05:11,150
(Canmore)

1527
01:05:14,220 --> 01:05:16,050
Where are we going now?

1528
01:05:16,050 --> 01:05:19,850
We need to throw ourselves into local culture in Calgary, Canada.

1529
01:05:19,850 --> 01:05:21,290
- Throw what?
- What are we doing?

1530
01:05:26,360 --> 01:05:27,830
What's here? We're here.

1531
01:05:27,830 --> 01:05:28,900
What is this?

1532
01:05:30,600 --> 01:05:33,000
Is it a bar? What is this place?

1533
01:05:33,530 --> 01:05:35,170
(Get ready for this.)

1534
01:05:35,370 --> 01:05:36,600
- Is it a pub?
- Oh, look.

1535
01:05:36,600 --> 01:05:40,270
That woman's shirt looks like something a bullfighter would wear.

1536
01:05:41,180 --> 01:05:43,240
My gosh, that parking lot is huge.

1537
01:05:43,240 --> 01:05:45,810
What's going on? Why are there so many cars here?

1538
01:05:45,810 --> 01:05:47,150
And it's full.

1539
01:05:49,050 --> 01:05:50,220
What's going on?

1540
01:05:50,220 --> 01:05:51,790
(Even the exterior has a rugged Wild West vibe.)

1541
01:05:53,090 --> 01:05:56,920
(Canadian charm in every corner)

1542
01:05:58,090 --> 01:06:00,360
Let's party the night away.

1543
01:06:00,360 --> 01:06:02,200
You can experience cowboy culture.

1544
01:06:02,960 --> 01:06:06,170
And it's the hottest spot in Calgary right now.

1545
01:06:06,600 --> 01:06:08,800
This neighbourhood seems deserted, but everyone's packed in here.

1546
01:06:08,800 --> 01:06:09,800
No wonder there were so many cars.

1547
01:06:09,800 --> 01:06:13,270
Even millennials and Gen Z are all here.

1548
01:06:13,270 --> 01:06:14,440
- Really?
- It's...

1549
01:06:14,440 --> 01:06:16,410
- A real hot spot.
- A hot spot.

1550
01:06:18,810 --> 01:06:20,080
What if they don't let us in?

1551
01:06:20,080 --> 01:06:21,320
Wait, where's the bouncer?

1552
01:06:22,180 --> 01:06:23,920
- Isn't this the entrance?
- Let's go. This way.

1553
01:06:24,490 --> 01:06:26,150
This way, please.

1554
01:06:28,560 --> 01:06:32,430
We like to party! Yes!

1555
01:06:32,430 --> 01:06:34,560
- What's this?
- Someone's excited already.

1556
01:06:35,200 --> 01:06:37,100
- Get your passports out.
- Passports.

1557
01:06:37,500 --> 01:06:38,670
- Hello.
- Hello.

1558
01:06:39,430 --> 01:06:40,740
Passport.

1559
01:06:41,670 --> 01:06:42,940
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1560
01:06:43,940 --> 01:06:45,770
- Let's go.
- My gosh.

1561
01:06:46,810 --> 01:06:48,110
- What is this?
- What is this?

1562
01:06:49,240 --> 01:06:52,050
- What is this place?
- Cowboys really are the theme.

1563
01:06:52,880 --> 01:06:57,620
(A cowboy club with a Wild West vibe)

1564
01:07:03,520 --> 01:07:04,890
(Exclaiming)

1565
01:07:05,430 --> 01:07:06,690
My gosh.

1566
01:07:06,690 --> 01:07:07,800
What is this?

1567
